{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/71921-crowd-sourcing-creativity","id":71921,"title":"Crowd Sourcing Creativity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-14T05:38:16-08:00","id":71921,"title":"Crowd Sourcing Creativity","content":"A message with at least ten characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":63,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/63-loxosceles","user":"Loxosceles","date":". 03-08-2014, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/63-loxosceles","name":"Loxosceles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T20:13:48-08:00","id":72428,"title":"","content":"- a snarling do gets involved, perhaps hindering the hindmost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:46:59-08:00","id":72590,"title":"","content":"Um...hm.<br /> <br /> --The quarry is a sewer rat or archaeologist intensely familiar with the city's sewers. He ducks into them and can make much better progress in the dark than the players can. Perception checks set a hard limit on how much distance the players can cover.<br /> --Alternately, the sewer is well-lit, but the players need to make Resolve rolls not to be sickened by what's in the air they're panting into their lungs.<br /> --The quarry knocks over an innocent bystander, maybe a small child, into the path of an oncoming horse who will trample him unless the player saves him. His level of success on a Panache roll minimizes the amount of lead the quarry gets from this distraction. It's kind of a stretch to call it a Panache roll, but since Panache is how many actions you get in combat, I'm going with it.<br /> --The chase leads through a private residence and through an area in which an innocent bystander is doing something private (undressing is the standard, but I don't know how much you want to do that trope). Roll Panache to not stumble, flustered by the embarrassment of what you just walked in on.<br /> --The quarry dives through a window. Roll Wits to think to pull your coat up to protect yourself before making the same jump or else suffer 1k1 damage from the glass you'll land on.<br /> --In an opera house or ballroom or something equally large, the quarry is springing along immense chandeliers like they're platforms in a Mario game to reach an opposite balcony. The heat coming off the chandeliers is surprisingly intense, and requires a Resolve roll to tolerate it or else take damage.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, that last one was goofy. I think I'm scraping the bottom of the barrel here. I'll come back with more if I think of 'em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:05:23-08:00","id":72713,"title":"","content":"The following examples were inspired from playing a few rounds of Space Station 13, but I think a few of them could work pretty much anywhere.<br /> <br /> -The Hallway is currently on Fire. A Fire Extinguisher might be a good idea, generally it's better to be faster than the fire.<br /> -The Hallway is currently the site of a breach and now being subjected to massive depressurization and oxygen loss.<br /> -The Hallway is Flooded with Toxic, hilariously unstable and flammable Plasma.<br /> -The Hallway has several Space Carp, as they generally come in via breaches this probably also means in addition to fleeing a pack of venomous space fish, you have to do it under earlier mentioned massive depressurization and oxygen loss.<br /> -The Hallway is now the home of Giant Spiders, who are venomous, pretty damn fast AND leave webs all over the place that slow you down even further. Should be noted, the webs can be torn apart with certain weapons, but the cheapest and fastest is fire, ideally from a welding tool.<br /> -Nuke Ops round and there are four or five heavily armed men with guns in the hallway. Actually fuck trying to run, just play dead after taking a few shots and hope they forget to double tap.<br /> -Space Vines have taken over the Hallway, they don't slow you down too badly, but there is zero visibility where it's thickest and they grow fast as hell.<br /> -Speaking of zero visibility, POWER OUTAGE! Find a Flashlight, rely on memory or following along the walls like real life blind people.<br /> -Can't believe I forgot this one, The Janitor hasn't discovered the wonders of Space Cleaner and has used water, trying to run on this floor will result in falling over and slipping<br /> -Janitor has washed the floor with Space Lube. Actually gets you across the hallway faster, if flat on your back, though this may lead to your untmely demise depending on what's on the other side of your journey<br /> -Either because its a Cult round and they've chosen you as a sacrifice or because it's a Rev Round and you're part of Command you're greatly outnumbered by hostile crew that are now chasing you.<br /> -This also applies to a Monkey Round, with the added bonus that Monkeys can pop out of the vents, fortunately they're a lot less sturdy than human crew.<br /> -Some wiseass has put Mindbreaker into all the air. You are now tripping like that one Kenny Rogers song.<br /> -The Gravitational Singularity is loose and is eating it's way through the Station! RUN LIKE HELL!<br /> -<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\">NAR-SIE HAS ARISEN!</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 02-15-2014, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T21:25:01-08:00","id":74093,"title":"","content":"- Chaser sees a crime taking place, like a mugging. Does he or she stop?<br /> <br /> - A look alike for the one being chased causes some confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}